Atlas overlay patch 0012: brand/about-updates-row
Why: Atlas has no updater of its own, so Settings > About must not offer to check for updates: the
 update status, the throbber and the relaunch button give way to one row, "Atlas updates with WolOS."
 and a link that opens the Software Update pane of WolOS System Settings (reel scene 11, R11). The
 link goes through a settings message to atlas::brand::OpenSoftwareUpdate(), which runs
 `wol-settings "Software Update"` (what the WolOS shell does for its update badge). No lower tier:
 the row is page markup and a message handler.
Files: chrome/browser/resources/settings/about_page/about_page.html.ts, about_page.ts, about_page_browser_proxy.ts,
 chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/about_handler.{h,cc}, chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_localized_strings_provider.cc
Test filter: *WolosRelease*; journey J-A9/R11 (About text, no "Check for updates" button, the link starts Software Update)
Rebase risk: M (about_page.html.ts is patched by about-page-tweaks and reenable-update-status; the hunk replaces the block those two edit)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

